WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.455
Ordinal encoding maps ordered categories to ordered
numbers The representation

00:00:06.481 --> 00:00:12.379
is compact and preserves rank But some analytical
methods may interpret

00:00:12.406 --> 00:00:18.088
the gaps between codes as equal That is an
additional assumption not

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:23.656
something guaranteed by the original category labels
Whenever you use

00:00:23.682 --> 00:00:29.642
ordinal codes document the intended order and
understand how the downstream model uses numeric
distance
